<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/North-Fields.jpg" alt="Plein air painting of the north fields at Ayrshire Farm in Upperville VA" width="450" height="323" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Ayrshire Farm North Fields. 5x7, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">There were so many things to take in at Ayrshire Farm today that I spent most of my time on photographs rather than actually painting.&nbsp;<span style="line-height: 1.42857;">As a squirrel gathers nuts, at this time of year I try to collect as much reference material as possible to get me through the winter months.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">After visiting with the pigs, horses, turkeys and a couple of foxes, I managed to make a small 5x7 sketch of the view across the fields to the north of the entrance driveway. I ran out of time (and energy) to do anything more substantial.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Sometimes it's easier to produce work at less picturesque locations.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>